    Open an image file and extract text using pytesseract OCR. If OCR result is empty,
    attempt to extract textual image comments/metadata (JPEG comment, EXIF UserComment, ImageDescription).
    The function returns a Python str (Unicode). If out_encoding is provided, the function
    returns bytes encoded with out_encoding.

    Parameters:
    - image_path: path to the image file
    - out_encoding: if None (default), return a Python str; if e.g. "utf-8", return bytes encoded in that encoding
    - tesseract_cmd: optional path to the tesseract executable (set pytesseract.pytesseract.tesseract_cmd)
    - lang: optional tesseract language code(s) (e.g. "eng", "eng+spa")

